.TH QFW-EXAMPLES 7 "August 2026" "QFw 0.1.0" "QFw Concepts"
.SH NAME
qfw-examples \- installed QFw application and integration tests
.SH DESCRIPTION
QFw installs its public example scripts beneath
.IR QFW_SHARE_DIR/examples .
They run after
.BR qfw-activate (1)
has prepared the shell. Change to that directory before using the command
forms shown in the example manual pages.
.PP
Backend-aware wrappers accept
.B --service-mode local
or
.BR --service-mode site .
Local mode selects the installed local runtime profile, starts the requested
application-owned QPM, runs the test, and tears down its runtime. Site mode
uses the installed site-only runtime and connects to an existing site-owned
QPM. Application teardown does not stop site services.
.PP
The activated
.B QFW_SITE_CONFIG
supplies site connection information. The
.B --site-config
and
.B --runtime-config
options provide per-invocation overrides. Applications do not need to create
a site-only runtime file.
.SH PREREQUISITES
Application-owned simulator runs require a scheduler allocation. Every node
participating in a multi-node or heterogeneous run must see
.B QFW_RUN_BASE_DIR
at the same pathname so PRTE and service coordination records are shared.
.PP
Site-mode runs require an active directory service and a compatible QPM. The
site configuration's directory connection record must be readable from the
application nodes.
.SH TESTS
.TP
.BR qfw_run_all.sh (1)
Run the backend-compatible test set and produce a pass, fail, and skip summary.
.TP
.BR qfw_qiskit_simple.sh (1)
Submit one measured Qiskit circuit.
.TP
.BR qfw_ghz.sh (1)
Run a Qiskit or PennyLane GHZ circuit.
.TP
.BR qfw_supermarq.sh (1)
Run a SuperMarQ GHZ or VQE workload through admission-managed capacity.
.TP
.BR qfw_chem_app.sh (1)
Run a QFw-enabled external chemistry application.
.TP
.BR qfw_mpi_smoke.sh (1)
Validate the specialized application-owned MPI service path.
.SH QUICK START
.EX
source /opt/openqse/qfw/current/bin/qfw-activate \e
  --venv /opt/openqse/qfw/venv
cd "${QFW_SHARE_DIR}/examples"

\&./qfw_run_all.sh --service-mode local --backend nwqsim \e
  --tests init-test,qiskit-simple,ghz-qiskit

qfw-deactivate
.EE
.SH RESULTS
Each wrapper emits a terminal
.B QFW_EXAMPLE_RESULT
record. When
.B QFW_EXAMPLE_RESULT_FILE
is set, the same records are appended as JSONL for automation.
.BR qfw_run_all.sh (1)
writes per-test logs, JSONL result files, and a combined
.I summary.jsonl
beneath
.BR QFW_RUN_BASE_DIR .
